-*- coding:utf-8 -*-

pi-constant-unbound — the AutoLISP constant PI evaluates to NIL in every dialect
================================================================================

Reported from: SCHMS+ CAD test harness (sncf-reseau/src/schms,
tests/test-cad.lsp) while porting it from BricsCAD to the clautolisp
mock host. clautolisp 1.7.18 / alfe 1.7.24, macOS.

Summary
-------

`pi` is a predefined constant in AutoLISP — 3.14159265358979 in both
AutoCAD and BricsCAD, in every context. Under clautolisp it is unbound
and evaluates to NIL, **in every dialect**, so any angle computation
silently becomes an error at the first arithmetic use.

    $ for d in strict lax clautolisp bricscad-v26 autocad-2022 ; do
        clautolisp --no-init --host mock --dialect $d \
                   -x '(princ (strcat "pi=" (vl-princ-to-string pi)))' -q
      done
    pi=nil
    pi=nil
    pi=nil
    pi=nil
    pi=nil

    $ alfe -norc --bricscad --mode batch \
           -x '(princ (strcat "\npi=" (vl-princ-to-string pi)))'
    pi=3.14159265358979

`(type pi)` is likewise NIL under clautolisp.

Symptom at the call site
------------------------

The failure surfaces far from the cause, because NIL propagates until
some arithmetic rejects it. In our case a stub file failed to load with

    [tu] WARNING: echec chargement source tests/bouchons-epure.lsp :
                  / expects a number, got NIL.

for a line that reads `(setq pi/2 (/ pi 2.0))` — nothing in the message
points at `pi`. Application code that does `(polar pt (+ ag pi) d)` will
fail the same way, one frame further in.

Expected
--------

`pi` is bound to the double-float value of π, in every dialect, with no
host required (it is a language constant, not a drawing property). It
should be non-writable, or at least behave like the vendors' — AutoCAD
and BricsCAD both allow `(setq pi 3)` and both restore it per-document,
so matching "bound by default" is the part that matters here.

Note that a bare `--dialect strict` run does not warn either: the symbol
is simply unbound, so nothing flags it. A dialect warning for a read of
an unbound symbol that the vendors define would have caught this at the
first use.

Why it matters
--------------

`pi` is used 97 times in the SCHMS+ sources alone, in every geometry
computation. Any AutoLISP application ported to clautolisp hits this on
its first angle, and the diagnostic points at the arithmetic rather than
at the missing constant. It is a one-line fix with a large blast radius.

Suggested test
--------------

A conformance case asserting `(equal pi 3.14159265358979 1e-14)` and
`(= (type pi) 'REAL)` on every backend, plus the vendor-parity probe for
the per-document reset behaviour if that is worth matching.

Related
-------

Found alongside the absence of `vla-get-activedocument` (already tracked
as an unchecked entry in issues/open/schms-call-inventory.md), which is
what currently stops the same SCHMS+ suite from running headless: it
makes src-vlx/plateforme.lsp fail to load, and with it
`schms_transaction_undo`, which every entity-mutating test goes through.

Resolved (clautolisp 1.7.25)
----------------------------
RESOLVED. `install-predefined-variables`
(autolisp-builtins-core/source/api.lisp) now binds the AutoLISP
predefined variables at engine start, in every dialect, with no host
required:

  - `PI`   -> `(coerce pi 'double-float)` = 3.141592653589793;
  - `T`    -> the AutoLISP true value;
  - `PAUSE`-> the "\\" command-pause string.

The binding is host-independent (a language constant, not a drawing
property) and writable, matching the vendors (both AutoCAD and BricsCAD
allow `(setq pi 3)`). `(print pi)` now prints the value in strict, lax,
clautolisp and every vendor dialect; the SCHMS+ geometry code (97 uses)
loads. Verified present on master at the time of this close.

Follow-up left open elsewhere (NOT part of this issue): a strict-dialect
diagnostic for a *read* of an unbound symbol that the vendors define —
tracked with the dialect-portability-warning work, not here.
